{"kind": "tool_approval", "tool": "book_chapter_save_draft", "args": {"body": "The air in the Great Library of Aethelgard was thick with the scent of ancient parchment and the faint, metallic tang of ozone. High above, the vaulted ceilings were lost in a swirling mist of magical residue, illuminated only by the rhythmic pulsing of the floating lanterns.

Kaelen moved through the shadows of the stacks, his footsteps muffled by the heavy velvet rugs. In his hand, he clutched a small, leather-bound volume that felt unnaturally warm against his palm. It was the Ember Codex—a relic whispered to be the heartbeat of the dying flame that sustained their world.

He reached the Restricted Section, where the shadows seemed to have teeth. The silence here wasn't just the absence of sound; it was a heavy, expectant thing, as if the books themselves were holding their breath, waiting for the spark that would either ignite the world or burn it to ash.", "book_id": "01a058c7-4f72-777a-8d44-dd84bc42091c", "chapter": "Chapter I — The Ember Codex", "chapter_id": "01a058c7-5002-7c9b-9d56-ad169644276a"}, "tier": "A"}

